    "clause_id": "c009",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The statement that staff decisions are \"imprecise and subject to errors in judgment\" comes close to characterising staff negligence as an inherent risk, and \"errors in judgment\" is exactly the kind of phrase parties dispute when a release is tested. Still, it is drafted as description, not as a disclaimer.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It sits against c016 (assumption of \"inherent\" risks) and c017, which releases negligence \"but not gross negligence or intentionally wrongful conduct\"; whether instructor misjudgment is an assumed inherent risk or released negligence is a real seam between those provisions. That is a plausible, though not certain, incoherence.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.26,
    "prob_cat2": 0.28
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c010",
    "reasoning_cat1": "\"On most NOLS courses\" and \"at times\" are hedged but the sentence is a factual disclosure with no operative effect. Nothing to construe.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It is consistent with c011's statement that NOLS cannot continually monitor students and with c016's assumption of risk. No conflict.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.05,
    "prob_cat2": 0.04
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c011",
    "reasoning_cat1": "This is an operative disclaimer buried in a descriptive risk list, and it turns on the undefined boundary of \"free time before, during and after their course\" and the fiction that accompanying staff act \"as private individuals\"; \"free\" is even placed in scare quotes, signalling its own indeterminacy. The disclaimer covers free time \"before and after\" the course while the preceding sentence also mentions free time \"during\" it, an internal mismatch a court could be asked to resolve.",
    "reasoning_cat2": "It must be read against c017, which releases claims \"arising in whole or part from enrollment or participation in an activity of NOLS,\" and the two draw the coverage line differently — c017 assumes NOLS-activity claims exist to be released while c011 asserts no responsibility at all. That mismatch, plus the tension with c018's reservation of authority over students, is a genuine relational risk.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.42,
    "prob_cat2": 0.34
  },
  {
    "clause_id": "c012",
    "reasoning_cat1": "The closing sentence that NOLS foreign field practices \"are generally consistent with customs and standards used in the United States\" is a hedged quasi-representation whose standard (\"generally consistent\") cannot readily be applied. The rest is descriptive listing with a catch-all (\"other criminal conduct\").",
    "reasoning_cat2": "The quasi-representation sits uneasily with c018's statement that admission is \"not intended as a representation\" and with the disclaimers in c011 and c014, but nothing directly contradicts it. Modest relational risk.",
    "prob_cat1": 0.19,
    "prob_cat2": 0.14
  }
]}

